{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_02cdb06a8ba24ea09df01eb813e9795d","id":"pg_934cbea3967d54e3af632bffa50cfe2e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/quinnod345-context-engine-awesome-list-submission-md-ff40183c8225-2bffa50cfe2e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e549867e3743553ab651a84a61b3e511"],"title":"Quinnod345/context-engine/awesome-list-submission.md @ ff40183c8225","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02cdb06a8ba24ea09df01eb813e9795d"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ee1877b255298700fc3ceab20ffa98073ad6bd574c91d49654b0c572b04179a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project positions itself for agents needing real-time situational awareness, semantic search over structured event streams, and quick prototypes with built-in temporal decay and deduplication."},{"claim_ids":["clm_172ff492b6da7011519f6f386e6da314825e9c1fe8172b12c6515ce5a5beed24"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Default embeddings use TF-IDF with locality-sensitive hashing projected to 128 dimensions, deterministic and network-free; an optional OpenAI text-embedding-3-small provider offers 1536-dimensional semantic search."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3375bd7d96c37283510074684d048f80fb8eadb3e7139066606bd023050a3f76"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports benchmarks on Apple Silicon with local TF-IDF and in-memory SQLite: roughly 0.1ms per ingest, 0.1ms per query across 1000 events, and about 20MB heap."},{"claim_ids":["clm_393e16452ac0102fa33cdb383582e16a025092145c30b744f6bf2ffb51581cfd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run npm install, npm run build to compile TypeScript, npm test for the test suite, and npm run dev for watch mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_62ac101334cc26dc67708e0ca602d248c3ffd7410fed72b2908d6e438b4343df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An MCP server example lets MCP-compatible clients such as Claude Desktop, Cursor, and Windsurf call ingest_event, query_context, get_recent, and clear_context as native tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a834fc855c29950e54cd13bb89643557b957fc3492d8223c4ce589c95dcb712b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The npm package context-engine-ai lets AI agents ingest events from any source and query them in natural language, returning ranked, time-decayed results without a vector database, API keys, or configuration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c3e0f3cecb7c769c587ee060ea186b6ee29890340a1e1adf613b58012535a04a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Query ranking multiplies cosine similarity by relevance and an exponential half-life decay factor 0.5^(age/halfLife), with a configurable decayHours defaulting to 24 hours."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c925389e44174a63b1ec3ee249137b688005b76fa8d38638435e34281f21adcf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The HTTP server mode exposes REST endpoints including POST /ingest, GET /context?q=..., GET /recent, GET /count, DELETE /events, and GET /health, startable via ctx.serve(3334) or an npx CLI command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d1c9ea2c49ed3db2b097bb569eecc7c5e2290c8818bf50b1dbcb221bfd8fed4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requirements are Node.js >= 18 with no external services in default configuration; PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension and an OpenAI API key are optional for production scale and higher-quality embeddings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d45a47f23e8857fcadb8367e30be2c8eae6ca6ed5cf4bd0fabe7c64048406dbc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the tool is not the right fit for searching large documents or PDFs, for months-long persistent memory, or for indexing millions of documents, suggesting RAG frameworks or dedicated vector databases instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d70d0317c3cd9762ab4916376e83f6bae00080a6381467626055aedb2db5ffdc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ingest deduplicates events whose cosine similarity exceeds a configurable threshold (default 0.95) within a time window (default 60s), merging timestamps, boosting relevance, and tracking a _mergeCount field."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed3a3be63b906075cb697552bc7f8c1f44a5bf1d5b1cf016a9fe43b4859d0b50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default the engine runs in-memory with events lost on restart; passing dbPath persists events to a standard SQLite file that survives restarts and can be inspected with SQLite tools."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ee1877b255298700fc3ceab20ffa98073ad6bd574c91d49654b0c572b04179a","clm_172ff492b6da7011519f6f386e6da314825e9c1fe8172b12c6515ce5a5beed24","clm_3375bd7